Research design and experimentation (@research-design-and-experimentation: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_46ZFQQBMNRDP7HA63J3B7AJR8H
Research design turns a question into a study capable of providing useful evidence. The material joins experimental controls, sampling, field observation, laboratory methods, simulation studies, and analysis planning, including reproducibility and the organisation of research with limited resources.

**Common preparation developed:** [Identification and selection investigation](../../core/Investigate-identification-selection-and-competing-causal-accounts.lingua) joins general conditional derivations with exact model comparisons, enumerated assignment laws, incomplete-outcome bounds and a bounded published reconstruction. Existing design/probability programs are reused unchanged. These checks do not establish causal validity for an actual study or observed learner competence; full research-design formation remains pending.

**Parent:** [Measurement and research](../Measurement-and-research.lingua#r_63SRHN81RMJ2MTA76HE11C5WR0).
} r_46ZFQQBMNRDP7HA63J3B7AJR8H
